35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: I found that the coordination group is still short-staffed, and the same two people write everything by hand.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: I found that half the customer plants lose network coverage for whole afternoons, which makes field work impossible.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"- **George**: The capital line is frozen, but the recurring software allowance still has room after those spring cancellations.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,- **May**: The last three rollouts show that anything needing daily entry from everyone was quietly dropped.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,- **Midori**: I found that the depot and planning office each lose nearly an hour daily just copying details that already exist elsewhere.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,- **Minato**: That is a lot of lost time. Does that mean the Supplier Data Hub would actually help stop the copying?,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: It is a valid question, but I worry about the technical feasibility given the network gaps I found.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"The recurring allowance covers software, but the capital freeze means we cannot fund major hardware or infrastructure changes.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""George"",""self"":true,""raw"":""George: The recurring allowance covers software, but the capital freeze means we cannot fund major hardware or infrastructure changes.""}]}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"That matches my findings. The tools that survived were narrow and specific, not broad systems requiring constant input.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""May"",""self"":true,""raw"":""May: That matches my findings. The tools that survived were narrow and specific, not broad systems requiring constant input.""}]}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,- **Midori**: That aligns with the misrouted deliveries I saw. The same address errors keep happening because records are scattered.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,- **Minato**: I also found that four standardization efforts ended without an owner. We need to ensure someone is actually responsible for this.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: My developer check confirms the risk. Both in-house staff are tied up until the third quarter, so we cannot build anything new.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"That confirms my pricing concern. Per-head licences will climb with every department, so we must avoid broad, multi-unit tools.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""George"",""self"":true,""raw"":""George: That confirms my pricing concern. Per-head licences will climb with every department, so we must avoid broad, multi-unit tools.""}]}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,- **May**: My vendor query check shows we request the same certificates repeatedly. A shared catalog would stop that waste immediately.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: The scattered records explain the misrouted deliveries too. If we centralize them, we stop both the copying and the errors.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: But if the coordination group is already overwhelmed, who will maintain the new hub? I worry about adding more work.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: That is a fair worry. With developers unavailable, we must pick a solution that does not require heavy new coding.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,Agreed. We must stay within the recurring software allowance. A fixed-fee build is safer than climbing per-head licence costs.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""George"",""self"":true,""raw"":""George: Agreed. We must stay within the recurring software allowance. A fixed-fee build is safer than climbing per-head licence costs.""}]}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,- **May**: Exactly. The narrow tools survived because they didn't demand constant input. We need something simple that doesn't rely on daily user discipline.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: I agree. A simple, shared catalog addresses the daily copying and errors without demanding constant new input from everyone.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
